  "description": "The abstract xUnit v3 contract suites every IOutboxStore, IInboxStore and IIdempotencyStore implementation must pass, so a custom store proves the same semantics as the built-in in-memory, EF Core, and Redis stores: atomic claims, claim tokens and leases, renewal, release, retries, dead letters and their operations, FIFO and partition order, the backlog, the inbox, idempotency claim tokens, stored results and payload fingerprints. Assertions use plain xUnit; no mocking or assertion library is forced on the consumer.",
